                        "sense_id": "08fc4450-81cc-34a4-bc2c-b7ca7945b6a5",
                        "entry_id": "11f5ca7b-5103-3260-8b9e-0d489bcfbce3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An alchemist, especially one who tried to discover remedies for diseases."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "49fb4633-1c44-4551-96ec-fc214a22e77e",
                                "sense_id": "08fc4450-81cc-34a4-bc2c-b7ca7945b6a5",
                                "text": "It has, of late more particularly, assumed not only an unforbidding, but even an engaging form, by the facility with which many of its most important researches are now conducted, and by the extension of them to numerous objects which had not before been attended to by the old spagyrists."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6fe20498-03e5-4e5b-bb9a-ff3b468fc7c2",
                                "sense_id": "08fc4450-81cc-34a4-bc2c-b7ca7945b6a5",
                                "text": "The Carmelite enjoyed the general amazement, and he told father and son how the secret of this substance had been revealed to him by an Arab; it was medicine far more powerful than the one Christian spagyrists called unguentum armarium."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed3f2e1a-bc67-41e2-bf8a-be83f0e05fbd",
                                "sense_id": "08fc4450-81cc-34a4-bc2c-b7ca7945b6a5",
                                "text": "Back when I was still a junior alchemist, passing through What Cheer, Iowa, met up with this old-school spagyrist name of Doddling, who showed me how to get silver to grow just like a tree."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
